;; Reviewed 2026-10-10 by the user (written by Claude, from design
;; section 16, the MACRO manual and the guest runs of tools/vax-suite).
;; Why this is right:
;; - Under -OC, the four things tools/vax-suite's first runs found.
;; - Shorter: SHORT of an INT8 is an INT8 again (voc's rule), so the
;;   parameter's byte is moved, MOVB, where CVTBB was written, which is
;;   no VAX instruction; CVTBL then widens it for RET, as before.
;; - Offset: the difference of two addresses, a longword computed in R0,
;;   returned as a quadword LONGINT: ASHL #-31, R0, R1 now gives it its
;;   high longword. Before, MoveInto saw R0 into R0 and did nothing, so
;;   R1 kept the second address (llvm-address-to-longint printed
;;   6665789243395 for 3).
;; - MakeDeep: NEW of 12 open dimensions. Each length store can take
;;   11 bytes, so past 11 a byte branch cannot skip them: BNEQ over
;;   JMP L^L_36, the label after the stores, where BEQL L_36 was
;;   (MACRO's BRDESTRANG for llvm-open-array-many-dimensions).
;; - RawBlock: SYSTEM.NEW(any, size), lowered as NEW was before, its
;;   size ignored. Now: the quadword size's high longword must be 0 and
;;   its low one positive, else trap 7 (PUSHL #7) at SYSTEM.NEW's line
;;   and column, then Allocate(size, 0) by CALLG with a list of two,
;;   tag 0 (CLRL), as LLVM's, and R0 stored through the VAR parameter.
; VaxWidenNew, written by poc (doc/developer/vax-macro32-backend.md)
	.TITLE	VAXWIDENNEW
